jobs.description:
Together with your colleagues, you ensure that goods are processed efficiently and accurately throughout the warehouse. You contribute to a safe and organised working environment while helping maintain a smooth flow of products.

• Loading and unloading trucks;
• Sorting goods and shipments;
• Picking orders;
• Packing and preparing orders for shipment;
• Processing incoming and outgoing goods;
• Checking products for quality and quantity;
• Maintaining a safe, clean and organised workplace;
• Supporting the efficient handling of daily logistics operations.

Functie-eisen:
This position is suitable for someone who enjoys physical work and feels comfortable in a warehouse environment. You work carefully, take responsibility for the quality of your work and are willing to work different shifts.

For this position:

• You have MBO-level working and thinking ability through education or experience;
• Experience in logistics is an advantage;
• You are physically fit and willing to perform manual tasks;
• You work accurately and pay attention to quality;
• You are flexible and willing to work in a 4-shift system;
• You have a good command of either Dutch or English;
• You preferably live within 25 kilometres of the work location and have your own transportation.

This is what you will do

You will be working at a large company in Zoetermeer where different types of meat products are produced that the whole of the Netherlands eats on their sandwich every morning. You can think of grill sausage, minced meat, filet american and much more! This organization has been active in the food industry for years and is a regular supplier of various supermarket chains throughout the Netherlands such as Jumbo, Lidl and Plus.

Within this company there is no slaughtering! The slaughtered meat within the production area is only processed into a final product that ends up in the supermarkets. This means you will be working in an environment where hygiene (NVWA and BRC) is very important!

As a Production Employee you will work together with your colleagues to produce various meat products according to the planning. The following tasks belong to your function:

- Packaging of meat products;
- Keeping track of the production process and assisting where necessary;
- Reading production receipts and planning;
- Checking articles for correct labels and shelf life;
- Producing according to the planning;
- Supplying machines;

You will be working in a day shift from Monday to Friday. The working hours may vary due to the supermarket orders. In any case, you will start at 06:00 or 07:00 in the morning and end your day between 15:00 and 17:00. After this you can enjoy the weekend and you are free!

This is who you are

- Living in the area of Rotterdam, Den Haag, Zoetermeer, Leiden, Waddinxveen, Capelle aan den IJssel, Alphen aan den Rijn or Woerden;
- Willing to work in a multicultural team;
- Willing to work fulltime and work overtime when there are rush orders;
- You speak the English or Dutch language;
- Able to perform work at a fast pace;
- You can be present every morning at 06:00 or 07:00.

As an Industrial Cleaning Specialist, your primary responsibility is to clean and prepare returned packaging materials for reuse. This includes removing stickers, barcodes, and labels, as well as occasionally disassembling and reassembling products. The job is both physically active and varied, offering you new challenges every day. If you thrive on being hands-on and enjoy an active role, this is the perfect opportunity for you.

Your key tasks include:

- Cleaning formwork and other packaging materials;
- Removing stickers, barcodes, and labels without damaging surfaces;
- Disassembling and reassembling products as needed.

You’ll work in two shifts: early (06:00–15:00) and late (15:00–00:00), ensuring flexibility and variety in your schedule.

- Proficiency in English;
- Physical fitness and ability to perform active work throughout the day;
- Availability for two-shift work without exceptions.
